<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd bought a total of 21,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat from Japanese trading house Mitsubishi Corp, traders said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Cheiljedang bought 10,500 tonnes at basis over May futures on the U.S grain futures markets including the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said. Shipment was set for March 5-April 5 to the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour bought the remaining 11,000 tonnes at flat purchase prices.</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follow:</p>
<p>Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Tonne(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		6,500   $154</p>
<p>(protein max 10.0%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		1,500   $152.60</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,200   $181.45</p>
<p>Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Bushel(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		3,300   $0.4651 (over CBOT's May)</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  800   $0.4256 (over CBOT's May)</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,000   $1.1191 (over KCBT's May)</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  3,400   $1.2203 (over MGE's May)</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
